 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505983,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Identify  a rational number between <span data-math=\"\\frac{7}{8}\">\\frac{7}{8}</span> and <span data-math=\"\\frac{{20}}{{21}}\">\\frac{{20}}{{21}}</span>.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You can use the density property process:</p>\n<p>Step 1: Add the two rational numbers.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{7}{8} + \\frac{{20}}{{21}} = \\frac{{7 \\times 21}}{{8 \\times 21}} + \\frac{{20 \\times 8}}{{21 \\times 8}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{147}}{{168}} + \\frac{{160}}{{168}}\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{307}}{{168}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: Divide that result by 2. Dividing by 2 is the same as multiplying by one-half.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{307}}{{168}} \\times \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{{307}}{{336}}\"></span></p>\n<p>There are other numbers, but this is the one found using this process.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Using the process from the chapter, <span data-math=\"\\frac{{307}}{{336}}\">\\frac{{307}}{{336}}</span> , and there are other answers."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
